{"key": "337fdc9b296ccc82", "role": "operator", "t": 1790963760.884, "seconds": 5.27, "output": "To solve this, we need to compare the two input strings and determine if they refer to the same function. \n\nWe can use a simple string comparison after normalizing the strings to remove any differences in case and to remove common words like \"Department\" that do not add to the uniqueness of the function.\n\n1. Normalize the strings by converting them to lower case and removing common words.\n2. Compare the normalized strings.\n\nLet's assume we have a function `normalize_string` that takes a string, converts it to lower case, and removes common words like \"department\".\n\n```python\ndef normalize_string(s):\n    common_words = [\"department\"]\n    s = s.lower()\n    for word in common_words:\n        s = s.replace(word, \"\").strip()\n    return s\n\ndef compare_functions(str1, str2):\n    norm_str1 = normalize_string(str1)\n    norm_str2 = normalize_string(str2)\n    if norm_str1 == norm_str2:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        return 0\n\nprint(compare_functions(\"NATURAL RESOURCES\", \"Natural Resources Department\"))\n```"}
